Rename to pim-config.json. Should contain a JSON object of this form:

{
    "subscriptions": {
        "NAME1": {
            "id": "SUBSCRIPTION-GUID",
            "aks_resource_group": "my-resource-group",
            "aks_cluster_name": "my-cluster",
            "roles": [
                "Role Display Name A",
                "Role Display Name B"
            ]
        },
        "NAME2": {
            "id": "SUBSCRIPTION-GUID-2",
            "aks_resource_group": "",
            "aks_cluster_name": ""
        }
    },
    "default_duration": "PT8H",
    "default_justification": "Development on Project"
}

Subscription entries can also be plain strings (just the ID) for activate-only use.
AKS fields are required for --switch mode.

Optional "roles" is an allowlist of PIM role display names to activate for that
subscription (exact, case-insensitive match). Omit it to activate all eligible
roles. The names must match verbatim what PIM reports -- run with --dry-run
(-DryRun in PowerShell) to print every eligible role's exact display name.
The --role / -Role CLI argument overrides this per-subscription filter.
